{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/852149-demon-1st-edition","id":852149,"title":"Demon - 1st edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-23T17:57:29-07:00","id":852149,"title":"Demon - 1st edition","content":"First, sorry for my English, not my first language. I will make some mistakes.<br /> <br /> So, I bought Demon without knowing what was really the God machine Chronicle setting. So, now, I have a 2nd edition books, and many, many 1st editions books. In summary, we have a 1st edition game with a changeling, a geist and a hunter, and I hope I can have some help to transform 2nd edition demon in 1st edition. The players will see some sparks of the demons/angels conflict.<br /> <br /> So, first, the experience cost:<br /> Primum will cost 8 x Dot, like all others supernatural powerstat, I guess.<br /> Embed and Exploid, hard to say. Must others surnaturels must pay a cost by dot. But not here. Any ideas ?<br /> Covers, I don't have any ideas either.<br /> Instead of 5 merits for one Primum dot, 3, like the others.<br /> <br /> Next questions: Demon powers need any modifications to play in the first editions ?<br /> <br /> Thanks for the help","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11511-winterfox","name":"WinterFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11511_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T18:30:47-07:00","id":852161,"title":"","content":"Embeds and Exploits cost the same amount of experience as two Merit dots each, so you could estimate around 6 xp per?<br /> <br /> A supernatural Morality trait generally costs (new dots x 3) xp, but the trick is the way the game metes out and regulates Cover beats. The road of least effort would be to just use the rules for Cover experiences as given, awarding 1 Cover xp for every end-of-session Cover beat, and 5 Cover xp for every Cover experience. I think that would hold up even after losing the beat gain from resolving Cover Conditions. Instead I'd take care to watch the effect scaling has on Cover. Scaling makes it easier for Unchained to stay stable at a low rating and avoid being Burned, or to build up new patchwork Covers (it takes a single minor pact and a single medial pact to take a demon from Cover 1 up to Cover 3 this way), but harder to claw up to a single strong and secure rating (every dot above Cover 5 now costs increasingly more compared to the base game). That could be good or bad in your eyes. It's certainly not unworkable, but if the idea of a stabler floor and a more distant ceiling doesn't sound right, you could just use the same flat costs as the base game, charging 15 Cover xp for each dot of Cover.<br /> <br /> Most of the rest should be fairly navigable. Don't skip the effects of Conditions, though, even if you're not using 2e's beat generation for resolving them. A lot of what would have been written as standard rules and situational modifiers in a 1e book gets folded into Conditions in 2e. Use your judgment. Demons are probably fine if they don't suffer Guilty, Shaken or Spooked after a compromise, similarly to how 1e vampires didn't suffer additional effects if they succeeded on a roll to maintain Humanity, but Demon isn't the same game without the threat of being Surveilled or Hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T18:58:50-07:00","id":852173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/852149-demon-1st-edition?p=852161#post852161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embeds and Exploits cost the same amount of experience as two Merit dots each, so you could estimate around 6 xp per?</div> </div> </div> </div>Too cheap. Most costs in second edition were calculated around the third dot of a first edition equivalent as part of &quot;levelling&quot; the previously exponential curve. So that would be more like 9-12 experience (depending on whether you use a skill dot or two merit dots as your point of reference).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T19:11:49-07:00","id":852178,"title":"","content":"Granted. I also somehow managed to overlook the most obvious preexisting example: <b>Mummy</b> is the other nWoD game with primarily non-dot-based powers, costing 15 flat for an Utterance, or 15/17 for an Affinity, and giving a starting character a comparable number of them (three Affinities and one or two Utterances). There's a little more going on, since you consider the cost of having individual Pillar ratings, but it seems like a good starting point.<br /> <br /> So, somewhere around 10 to 15. Maybe 10/12 if you want to introduce a favored/unfavored divide to Demon, charging less for your Incarnation's associated category of Embeds. (Comfortably, even Analysts from the supplement books are covered by this: they get to favor Exploits.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T11:21:21-07:00","id":854564,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> So Primum: 8 x Dot, Embeds and exploits, 12 each, and covers, keep covers xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11511-winterfox","name":"WinterFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11511_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:51:34-07:00","id":854736,"title":"","content":"1 Beat is equal to 1 first edition experience point in terms of buying power, so Embeds and Exploits should cost 10 exp each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}